\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Must a contractible complex manifold with a complete smooth Kähler metric satisfying $-B\leq sec\leq -A<0$ for finite positive $A\leq B$ admit a bounded holomorphic map into $C^{n}$ with everywhere nonzero complex Jacobian, where n is its complex dimension?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Must a contractible complex manifold with a complete smooth Kähler metric satisfying $-B\leq sec\leq -A<0$ for finite positive $A\leq B$ admit a bounded holomorphic map into $C^{n}$ with everywhere nonzero complex Jacobian, where n is its complex dimension?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.11379}.
